    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely! That's a great idea, especially if you're new to weight training and don't have a lot of experience yet. Here's a less intense 4-week plan focusing on squats, bench press, and deadlifts with a very low starting weight. You can perform the exercises using just your bodyweight or light weights, like a dumbbell or backpack filled with books! \n\nWeek 1\nSquats with dumbbells: hold a seatbelt for less than 10 lbs\nBench press with dumbbell: hold a can of soda for less than 10 lbs (no lockout needed, just edge if you can't press it yet)\nDeadlifts with dumbbells: hold a can of soda for less than 10 lbs (if you can't lift the weight, just hold the book bag your heart rate)\n\nWeek 2\nSquats with dumbbells: hold a seatbelt for more than 10 lbs but less than 15 lbs\nBench press with dumbbell: hold a can of soda for more than 1 but less than 2 lbs\nDeadlifts with dumbbells: hold a can of soda for more than 1 but less than 2 lbs\n\nWeek 3\nSquats with dumbbells: hold a seat",
